1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,696
AI can recognise what's in a photo.

2
00:00:03,746 --> 00:00:06,650
But can it prove what's true?

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,717
Installations are signed off on photos and checklists.

4
00:00:10,767 --> 00:00:17,650
But a cable you can see is not proof that the right two ports are connected.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,906
Image AI asks: what's in this picture?

6
00:00:21,956 --> 00:00:27,650
ProofCam asks: what evidence establishes this requirement, and what's still missing?

7
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:36,650
This is ProofCam: an AI agent that inspects physical installations, decides what it still needs to see, and asks for that exact view.

8
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:41,130
First, a failure case, on AI-generated test photos.

9
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:45,010
The requirement: a blue cable into LAN 1.

10
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:53,740
Muse Spark reads the port labels, SAM grounds the plug, and the policy sees LAN 1 clearly empty.

11
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:54,225
Violated.

12
00:00:54,275 --> 00:00:56,165
Not ‘looks plugged in’.

13
00:00:56,215 --> 00:00:56,650
Violated.

14
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,546
Every photo re-evaluates every requirement.

15
00:00:59,596 --> 00:01:09,650
When a fact is missing, like whether one cable joins both ends, ProofCam plans the next camera view to close that gap.

16
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:12,643
Two Meta models, one system.

17
00:01:12,693 --> 00:01:17,429
Muse Spark reasons: photos become structured claims and next-view plans.

18
00:01:17,479 --> 00:01:21,736
SAM 3.1 grounds those claims in real pixels.

19
00:01:21,786 --> 00:01:23,650
A deterministic policy decides.

20
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:31,841
Now my real setup: a Jio set-top box, a PlayStation 5 and a TV.

21
00:01:31,891 --> 00:01:32,926
Four photos.

22
00:01:32,976 --> 00:01:39,432
Each time, Muse observes, SAM segments, and the policy re-checks both connections.

23
00:01:39,482 --> 00:01:43,228
Three plug ends are established from photos.

24
00:01:43,278 --> 00:01:48,650
One HDMI plug Muse saw, but SAM could not confirm.

25
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:52,228
That is where ProofCam stays honest.

26
00:01:52,278 --> 00:02:02,650
When the camera can't prove something, it says so, and records exactly what I confirmed, labelled as human, not as vision.

27
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,697
The result: verified, operator-attested.

28
00:02:05,747 --> 00:02:13,650
Every claim links to a photo, a model output or a time-stamped statement.

29
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:24,650
Under the hood: structured model outputs, policy-only verdicts, an append-only evidence store, call budgets, and over five hundred automated tests.

30
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:26,941
Today it's cables.

31
00:02:26,991 --> 00:02:37,650
But the same loop, requirement, evidence, verification, audit trail, could serve data centres, telecom, factories, energy and field maintenance.

32
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:46,650
What if every physical installation could explain why it was trusted?

33
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,307
ProofCam.

34
00:02:48,357 --> 00:02:50,421
Muse reasons.

35
00:02:50,471 --> 00:02:52,536
SAM grounds.

36
00:02:52,586 --> 00:02:54,650
Policy verifies.
